---
functor: 1
title: Math basics
---

set heading(numbering: none)

Inline math is between two dollar signs: `$x + y$`. Display math is between two lines of `$$`. Math uses names, not backslashes.

# Names and spaces

A space separates two names. `d x` is d times x. A word that is not a name shows as single letters, with a warning and a hint.

| Write | Result | Note |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `a b c` | $a b c$ | three letters |
| `2 x + 1` | $2 x + 1$ | numbers are upright |
| `3.14` | $3.14$ | a decimal point |
| `sin x` | $sin x$ | a function name is upright |
| `alpha + Omega` | $alpha + Omega$ | Greek |
| `x in A` | $x in A$ | a relation |

Single letters are italic. The signs `+ - * = < > , ; : ! / |` work as they are, and `-` is a true minus sign.

# Scripts and primes

| Write | Result |
|:--|:-:|
| `x_1`, `x^2` | $x_1, x^2$ |
| `x_(i + 1)^(n - 1)` | $x_(i + 1)^(n - 1)$ |
| `a_(i j)` | $a_(i j)$ |
| `f'`, `f''`, `f'''` | $f', f'', f'''$ |
| `e^(i pi)` | $e^(i pi)$ |

A script is one item or a group in round brackets. Two `_` on one term is an error: put both parts in one group.

# Groups and brackets

Round brackets group and show. `x_(i + 1)` uses the brackets as a group only. `(a + b)^2` shows them. Square and curly brackets also show.

| Write | Result |
|:--|:-:|
| `(a + b)^2` | $(a + b)^2$ |
| `[0, 1]` | $[0, 1]$ |
| `{x}` | ${x}$ |
| `(frac(a, b))` | $(frac(a, b))$ |

Brackets grow with the content. Each bracket must close with its own kind, so a half-open interval such as `[0, 1)` has no form yet. A group can take operations: `(a + b).bar`, `(F_T).box`. See [Recipes](symbols/recipes.html).

# Text in math

Text in quotes is upright: `"if"`, `"tr" A`.

```fn
$f(x) = 0 quad "for all" quad x in R.bb$
```

# Limits

`sum`, `prod`, `union`, `inter`, `lim`, `max` and `min` put their scripts below and above in display math, and at the side in text. `integral` puts them at the side.

```fn
$$
sum_(k = 1)^n k = frac(n (n + 1), 2),   lim_(n to infty) (1 + frac(1, n))^n = e,   integral_0^1 x^2 d x = frac(1, 3)
$$
```
